class Solution {
  public int undoDrawerBossReceipt(int[] readings, int k) {
    int[] a=readings; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {for(int x:a){if(x>=0)out.add(x);else for(int i=0;i<-x&&!out.isEmpty();i++)out.remove(out.size()-1);}}
    int answer=0;for(int i=0;i<out.size();i++)answer+=(i+1)*out.get(i);return answer;
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

A nonnegative event pushes that value onto a stack. A negative event removes up to abs(event) values from its top. Produce the final stack from bottom to top.

Return the weighted sum of the derived sequence: multiply its first value by 1, its second by 2, and so on, then add the products. Return 0 for an empty sequence.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n); space O(n).

